   "source": [
    "### Interpreting the Coefficients\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Linear regression:** a coefficient tells us how much the predicted fare changes per unit increase in the feature. The negative age coefficient means older passengers paid slightly less fare on average; the large negative `Pclass` coefficient shows that moving from 1st to 3rd class (increasing numeric `Pclass`) sharply reduces the expected fare.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Logistic regression:** the coefficients correspond to log‑odds of survival. Taking the exponential gives odds ratios. For example, the `Sex` coefficient of roughly 2.53 implies odds of survival for females are about `exp(2.53)≈12.6` times the odds for males, while a `Pclass` coefficient of -1.25 reduces survival odds (odds ratio ≈0.29).\n",
    "\n",
    "These interpretations help us understand feature impact on the predictions."
   ]
